        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>Warp yarns or fabric is wound onto a perforated beam. The dye liquor is forced through the perforations on the inside of the beam to the outside (and viceversa) to impart color.  The fabric remains stationary while the liquor is forced through increasing presure. This type of machine is used mainly for dyeing polyester and polyester blended fabrics that require high temperature and pressure.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
